  "overview": "**Aviva Standards** is a light-first design system anchored on `#ffffff` canvas surfaces with `#0b0b0c` primary ink (19.7:1 contrast) and `#ffd900` brand accent.\n\nTypography centers cleanly on `System Sans` (56px display down to 14px body), unified by `.25em` base corner radius and subtle shadow elevation.\n\nMaintained by **Aviva**. Source: live stylesheet extraction (https://standards.aviva.com/). Inventory: **22** colors, **48** typography steps, and **44** documented components (all rights reserved license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 44 component tokens with documented paddings: `0`, `0 1em 1em`, `1em 2em`, `.75em 1.25em`, `.2858em 0`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `#ffffff` cards; separate sibling sections using `#c6c6c6` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Layered Shadow Model**: Uses documented shadows (`inset 0 2px 2px 0 hsla(0,0%,80%,.5)`, `0 2px 2px 0 hsla(0,0%,80%,.5)`) paired with `#c6c6c6` borders for elevated overlays.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `#ffd900` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `#ffffff` (light) with `#0b0b0c` primary text and `#0b0b0c` secondary labels.\n- Use `#ffd900` with `#0b0b0c` text (14.2:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `System Sans` headings with `System Sans` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Apply `.25em` base geometry across inputs and buttons (.25em on outer containers).\n- Separate containers via `#ffffff` surface shifts and `#c6c6c6` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of light polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not mix conflicting corner radii that clash with the system's `.25em` baseline.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `textarea` fields and secondary buttons."
}
